  "note": "In-game ?bench=all sweep by the user (his machine, in-browser, vsync-capped 120 Hz - ocean-horizon sits at 120 fps / 8.33 ms) against the FIRST build/original/opensa in which ALL 212 mod cars are the high-poly fleet (30k-100k polygons each; earlier sweeps carried a partial replacement) - the 2026-08-17 rebuild: pak world.ospak 1 269 600 256 B, 1124 cell entries, buildTime 2026-08-17 ~10:54, vehicles.img 1781 MB + vehicles2.img 1415 MB of .osm, fetch-pack 129 chunks; the map itself also moved since the last capped sweep (2026-08-09): mods 64/65 (GTA5 cranes, Watts towers), Map Fixes col repairs, the LOD-visibility fixes (split order, one atomic per objs row, pow2 DXT resample), Urbanize IPL fold, 2dfx at LOD range. Road cars registered as usual (~1 219; peren at 1323,-1454 refused 300 spawns - 'no ground yet' - the known deferred-spawn class). legStart.ok true on all 9 rows, lateCreates 0, no CLEO/console errors beyond one 'atlas miss: read 0x18'. COMPARABILITY: capped lane, so avgMs/p95Ms sit on the vsync period wherever the GPU allows; the baseline is 2026-08-09-headless-bench-aa-after-102.json arm1 (Claude, headless drive.js, DPR=2, capped, the 2026-08-08 13:19 pak) - a different harness surface and an 8-days-older map, so the delta below is BUILD + FLEET + surface, not the fleet alone.",
  "analysis": "Against 08-09 arm1: no city scene holds 120 fps any more - ls-noon 8.3->11.5 ms (gpu.pass 2.7->6.9), sf-fog-dawn 8.3->10.3 (2.5->5.4), lv-night 8.3->17.2 (3.6->11.8, 58 fps), country-dusk 8.3->16.3 (3.8->12.4, 61 fps), ls-rain-night 8.3->10.5 (2.7->5.9), ganton-noon 8.3->15.2 (3.1->10.4), strip-noon 8.3->12.1 (3.2->7.3), ganton-night 8.3->15.7 (3.2->10.8); ocean-horizon unchanged (2.3->2.2). GPU pass x2.5-3.3 everywhere with content, CPU-side systems flat (vehicles meanMs 0.28-0.45 as before, fixed/physics 1-3 ms). What the fleet CAN explain: avgTriangles +50-100 % on car-heavy scenes (ls-noon 2.31M->3.91M, lv-night 2.06M->4.25M, ganton 1.57M->3.14M) and draws +50-80 %. What it CANNOT: country-dusk holds 4 cars, tris +18 %, draws +8 %, and its gpu.pass still triples (3.8->12.4) - and cellVertex residency is 2.0-2.9x on EVERY scene (150-228 -> 349-516 MB-units), texture residency +15-25 %. So a large share of the regression is the WORLD (what the map contains and how much of it is resident), not the cars. NEXT MEASUREMENT (before any fix): the same sweep on the same pak with ?benchcar=<one stock low-poly model> pins every road car to one cheap model - if gpu.pass falls back near 3-4 ms the fleet is the cost; if country-dusk stays at ~12 the world is. Then a rect repack / model-repack A/B on the suspect map layer. UNCAPPED=1 headless is the lane for the cost question; this capped in-game run answers 'does it hold 120' (no).",
